<title>USA: Safeway sets debt refinancing.</title>
<headline>Safeway sets debt refinancing.</headline>
<dateline>OAKLAND, Calif. 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Safeway Inc Monday commenced tender offers to acquire $870.9 million of its outstanding public debt and filed a shelf registration for $1.0 billion of new debt as part of a refinancing package.</p>
<p>In a statement, the operator of a national chain of grocery stores said the refinancing of substantially all of its public long-term debt is designed to reduce interest expense, extend maturities and enhance financial flexibility.</p>
<p>Safeway said it will pay prices equal to the greater of a fixed price or an amount based on the spread of prices for applicaable U.S. Treasury securities.  </p>
<p>The tender offers expire at 1700 EDT/2100 GMT September 4, unless extended.</p>
<p>Safeway intends to finance the debt buyback with proceeds from a new debt offering, loans under its bank credit line, commercial paper or by using a combination of the three.</p>
